    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9a13e4e2-c7ef-5f30-8a9a-1af61c6951e6",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ is a solution of $Ax=0$?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=4 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\nSince $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0$, the nullspace contains a nonzero vector. Thus $A$ is not invertible. This does not determine its exact rank or nullity.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)<4$, $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne\\mathbb{R}^{4}$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$ is false. $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$.\n\n- Statement $A\\text{ is invertible}$ is false. $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}$ is true. $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne \\mathbb{R}^{4}$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}$ only.",
